 "issue": 1839,
 "issue_title": "Bug: preserve all-null pandas nullable Float64 dtype",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\nAll-null pandas nullable `Float64` extension columns lose their numeric dtype when round-tripped through `from_pandas()` and `to_pandas()`.\n\n## Why it matters\nUsers who rely on pandas nullable extension dtypes expect an all-null `Float64` column to remain a nullable numeric column, the same way all-null `Int64` and `boolean` columns are currently preserved. Returning `string` can break downstream schema validation, numeric selection, Arrow/Parquet export assumptions, and ML preprocessing pipelines that depend on numeric dtype metadata.\n\n## Evidence\n- `arnio/convert.py`: `_pandas_dtype_to_arnio()` preserves `pd.Int64Dtype()` and `pd.BooleanDtype()`, but does not recognize pandas nullable `Float64Dtype()`.\n- `tests/test_convert.py`: `test_from_pandas_all_null_float64_extension` currently documents the resulting pandas dtype as `string`.\n- Local verification on `origin/main` shows:\n  - all-null `Int64` -> Arnio `int64` -> pandas `Int64`\n  - all-null `boolean` -> Arnio `bool` -> pandas `boolean`\n  - all-null `Float64` -> Arnio `string` -> pandas `string`\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n1. Create an all-null pandas nullable float column:\n   ```python\n   import pandas as pd\n   import arnio as ar\n\n   df = pd.DataFrame({\"score\": pd.Series([pd.NA, pd.NA], dtype=\"Float64\")})\n   frame = ar.from_pandas(df)\n   result = ar.to_pandas(frame)\n   print(frame.dtypes)\n   print(result.dtypes)\n   ```\n2. Observe that `score` becomes `string` instead of a nullable/float numeric dtype.\n\n## Expected behavior\nThe all-null nullable `Float64` column should keep numeric intent across the round-trip, ideally as Arnio `float64` and pandas `float64`/nullable-compatible output with nulls preserved.\n\n## Actual behavior\nThe column is inferred as Arnio `string` and returns to pandas as `string`, even though the original pandas dtype was explicitly `Float64`.\n\n## Suggested direction\n- Teach `_pandas_dtype_to_arnio()` to recognize pandas nullable float extension dtypes, at minimum `pd.Float64Dtype()`.\n- Add focused tests for all-null and mixed-null nullable float columns.\n- Revisit the existing all-null nullable float test so it asserts the intended numeric behavior instead of documenting the current lossy behavior.\n\n## References\n- `arnio/convert.py`\n- `tests/test_convert.py`\n- Related but not duplicate: #625 added coverage for current all-null extension behavior; this issue tracks the implementation fix.",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1839",
 "pr": 1984,
 "pr_title": "fix: preserve Float64 nullable dtype in from_pandas round-trip",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\r\nTeach `_pandas_dtype_to_arnio()` to recognise `pd.Float64Dtype()`, mirroring the existing `Int64Dtype` and `BooleanDtype` handling. All-null nullable `Float64` columns now round-trip as `float64` instead of `string`.\r\n\r\n## Linked issue\r\nFixes #1839\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n- [x] Bug fix\r\n\r\n## Area\r\n- [x] pandas interoperability\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n- [x] Other: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_convert.py -v -k \"float64\"` - 2 passed, 1 skipped (pyarrow not installed)\r\n\r\n## Contributor checklist\r\n- [x] I read the contributing guide.\r\n- [x] I kept the PR focused on one issue or one logical change.\r\n- [x] I added or updated tests for behavior changes.\r\n- [x] I checked that generated files, logs, and local build artifacts are not committed.\r\n- [x] My PR title uses Conventional Commits (`fix:`).",
